  "knowledge": [
    {
      "id": "k-scope",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "Everything that doesn't give off its own light looks projected, all from the orb: the UI, Cori's plate, the moth and Cori. Text the least, so it reads."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-source",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "The projection comes from the orb: scanlines and noise are measured from it, not laid flat over the screen.",
      "why": "User: \"it should emit from the orb, should be more like scanlines / procedural noise.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "k-recipe",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "Recipe: fine ring scanlines from the orb on surfaces only (1px / 3px, 7%, slow outward drift); low-frequency procedural noise on edges as a slow shimmer / buzz, growing with distance from the orb (0.5 → 2.5px); the pulse is the update: a ring from the orb that draws things in and gives the noise a new pattern, on appear, section change, Cori landing and every ~12 s. The pulse lights everything it passes: the line, the corner ticks and a glow, in a band around the ring.",
      "why": "User: rings finer; noise a slow shimmer/buzz; a pulse changes/updates it."
    },
    {
      "id": "h-numbers",
      "kind": "hypothesis",
      "text": "Numbers to tune on screen: ring pitch 3px at 7%, pulse every ~12 s, noise 0.5 → 2.5px."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-dropped",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "Too noisy, dropped: grain, colour split, tear, rolling band, whole-screen flicker."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-text",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "Text never warps; the scanlines pass under it on the surface. Contrast (WCAG AA) is measured without the effect."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-calm",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "Calm: rings and noise hold still, no timed pulse; an event pulse becomes a fade."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-rail",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "The rail (nav bar) is a projection too and stays: rings, shimmer and pulse as on every surface."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-dropout",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "Dropouts: now and then (every ~5–18 s per part, more often farther from the orb) one side of a frame's line or one corner tick flickers out and comes back (~0.4–1 s). Text never. Calm: none.",
      "why": "User, 2026-11-22: \"flicker in and out in some places, maybe the borders or a corner or two flicker out, and come back.\""
    },
    {
      "id": "k-draw-in",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "The pulse rewrites the page in place: a switch keeps the windows (the 1st Frame becomes the 1st Frame, pinned pieces stay) and each one's content turns into the new as the ring from the orb reaches it, nearest first; only a first visit draws the page in from faint. Cori stays where she was. Calm: the plain fade.",
      "why": "User, 2026-11-22: \"have the pulse draw in the new page... that is how the UI works, so it needs to follow the continuity.\" User, 2026-11-22: the reset between page switches was too much; \"the pulse comes through and rewrites/updates the projections.\""
    }
  ],
  "agent": {
    "brief": "One projection effect for every overlay element, sourced at the orb. Never on the sky.",
    "rules": [
      "Scanlines: a repeating-radial-gradient centred on the orb (CSS vars --orb-x/--orb-y set from the orb's rect), as a background layer on Frame, Plate, Button and the rail; animate the gradient offset slowly (background-position or a registered @property).",
      "Noise: one SVG filter (feTurbulence baseFrequency ≈ 0.01, feDisplacementMap) on line/border layers only; scale from distance to the orb (near / mid / far classes, not per frame); the shimmer = a slow baseFrequency drift; each pulse sets a new seed as it passes.",
      "Pulse: one expanding ring element from the orb (transform: scale), with an IntersectionObserver-free timing: each element's draw-in delay = its distance to the orb / pulse speed.",
      "Game: same origin (the orb's screen position) for HUD rings; sky layers untouched.",
      "prefers-reduced-motion: no drift, no noise animation, pulse → opacity fade."
